for many the new year symbolizes a fresh  start and a time to set resolutions and  over the next few months many gyms and  studios see an influx of people who  want to get fit eight news now reporter  kate houston spoke to the owner of a  local meal prep business  about the importance of nutrition when  it comes to achieving your goals  it's very important to plan ahead and  that's what we're here for  andrew portergalidad is the head chef  and owner of the good life meal prep  a las vegas business offering healthy  cooked meals that are delivered to a  customer on a weekly basis  they don't have to think about it it's  peace of mind they have a  healthy nutritious balanced meal  ready to go in the refrigerator when the  day gets busy  like clockwork protogallidad says he  always sees a bump in sales the week  after new year's  when it comes to fitness resolutions  nutrition is just as essential as  hitting the gym  as far as tackling exercise goals  running goals  lifting goals you're going to need that  extra nutrition so  it's important to stay on top of all  that while meal prep is great for those  solely focusing on fitness  puerto gallidad adds that this model is  just as helpful for busy moms and dads  trying to balance their health and  taking care of their kids  sometimes when you're cooking for other  people and taking care of other people  you just need a little help  at the end of the day or in the middle  of the day someone  that has your back and is going to take  care of you as many head into the new  year with a focus on wellness  puerto gallidad says it's important to  stay consistent both in the gym  and the kitchen it's important that when  you're setting your goals  you have a plan of attack and then you  stick to those kate houston  8 news now the good life team rotates  its menu based on what's in season the  goal of each meal is to be balanced and  familiar to most customers  there are options for all ages including  kids as well
 

